tray-host-polish: full first tray menu on GTK trays, leave a menu those trays never close, program names in notifications

What he saw (patch 123/124 on XFCE (labwc + xfce4-panel) and waybar): the first right-click on a Wine tray icon draws a
placeholder-sized menu with a scroll arrow (the full menu only from the second open); after a menu is dismissed the
program stays stuck in its menu until the next right-click; balloon notifications are titled with the tooltip's first line
or the item id instead of the program's name.

Mechanism:
1. libdbusmenu/GTK trays (xfce4-panel, waybar; Cinnamon's xapp-sn-watcher shows the same pattern) draw the layout they
   hold the moment the user clicks and send AboutToShow as a notification; an xdg_popup cannot grow after it maps. On a
   fresh icon the layout is empty until the program is asked for its menu, which Windows does only on the click.
2. Those trays never send the dbusmenu "closed" event (bus monitor: only "clicked"; no "opened"/"closed" on XFCE,
   waybar, Cinnamon), so TrackPopupMenu kept waiting for the tray's answer.
3. The notification app name came from the tooltip.

Fix:
1. explorer remembers each program's last tray menu (HKCU\Software\Wine\Explorer\TrayMenus, keyed by the exe path,
   written when the tray accepts a menu) and hands it to the driver right after NIM_ADD as a request-0 menu; winewayland
   attaches it as the icon's starting layout (only for an idle icon that uses dbusmenu, never over a live menu) and
   emits LayoutUpdated, so the tray holds the real layout before its first draw. Every click still asks the program,
   as Windows does, and replaces it. No host is stalled: nothing waits on the bus.
2. While TrackPopupMenu waits for the tray it sets __wine_systray_menu_active on its window to the request; the tray's
   result is applied only while it matches. A button press or key press in the program (the menu being gone: a tray
   menu holds the input while open) ends the wait with 0, the way the menu closing does on Windows; the message is
   dispatched normally. The next right-click still supersedes an old request.
3. explorer stores the program's name (version info FileDescription, else ProductName, else the exe name) as a global
   atom property on the icon's window on the first balloon; winewayland uses it as the notification's app name
   (fallback: the tooltip's first line, then the item id).

Windows: the tray asks the program for its menu only on the click (WM_CONTEXTMENU); the program's own menu is open
until it closes, then TrackPopupMenu returns; the notification shows the program's display name (FileDescription).

Not covered:
- The first right-click ever for a program (nothing remembered yet) still shows the tray's placeholder on XFCE/waybar.
- An app-drawn tray menu (patch 125's layer surface) does not close on a click on the empty desktop on sway or
  Hyprland: the compositor gives Wine no event (0 Wine input events after the click, +keyboard,+waylanddrv,+win, sway).
  Clicks on another window, Escape and choosing do close it. The Wayland-native fix would be an xdg_popup with a grab on
  an invisible layer-surface parent (the compositor then dismisses it); not attempted here.
- waybar never gives a click point on right-click (no ContextMenu even with Menu "/NO_DBUSMENU"), so an app-drawn menu
  opens at the last known point: after any left-click (Activate x,y) it is at the click; before one it is at Wine's
  last cursor position (0,0 in a fresh session).
- Programs that never call TrackPopupMenu (their own popup) are unaffected by 1 and 2.

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-181t = 181 + this patch; traytest v4, its own tray test program):
- First open, fresh session: XFCE 182 device rows (2/2) vs 26 with NEUTRON_TRAY_MENU_MEMORY=0 (1/1); Hyprland/waybar
  140 rows, First/Second/Quit (2/2) vs 38 rows, the scroll-arrow placeholder, with the switch (2/2); Cinnamon full
  menu at the icon on the first open (1/1).
- Leaving a menu the tray never closes: click into the program's window -> "menu returned 0" in the same millisecond:
  XFCE 2/2, Hyprland 2/2; NEUTRON_TRAY_MENU_INPUT_END=0 on the same build: the click does not end it, the next
  right-click does (XFCE 1/1, Hyprland 1/1). Choices still return their command (Cinnamon "Second" -> 2).
- Notification app name "Tray Test Program" (FileDescription) (XFCE m1, GNOME g2); exe without version info -> "traytest-nv".
- Regression: GNOME (nested devkit, AppIndicator 66): first open full, at the icon (g2); right-click + Escape behaves the same on 181 (g4) and 181t (g3): see the note below; Plasma 6 (nested, 126): the app's own menu at the click, Escape 0, second right-click the own menu again, never re-announced (1/1).

Pre-existing, not this patch (GNOME devkit rig): after right-click + Escape the icon vanishes from the top bar and the
program stays in TrackPopupMenu until it exits; identical on 181 and 181t (1/1 each), unverified on a real GNOME session.

Kill switches: NEUTRON_TRAY_MENU_MEMORY=0 (explorer: no remembered menus), NEUTRON_TRAY_MENU_INPUT_END=0 (the program's
input no longer ends a tray menu wait).
Files: include/ntuser.h, dlls/win32u/menu.c, programs/explorer/systray.c, programs/explorer/Makefile.in (version),
dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_sni.c.


--- a/dlls/win32u/menu.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/menu.c
@@ -4700,6 +4700,26 @@
 
 static const WCHAR tray_menu_propW[] = WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_PROP_INIT;
 static const WCHAR tray_menu_resultW[] = WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_RESULT_PROP_INIT;
+static const WCHAR tray_menu_activeW[] = WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_ACTIVE_PROP_INIT;
+
+/* NEUTRON tray-host-polish: the user is back in the application: a button press or a key in one of its windows.
+ * While the desktop's tray shows the menu it holds the pointer and the keyboard, so such input means the menu is
+ * gone; trays that never say "closed" (XFCE's panel, waybar) left the application waiting until the next right
+ * click. Windows ends a menu loop on a click elsewhere with 0. Kill switch NEUTRON_TRAY_MENU_INPUT_END=0. */
+static BOOL tray_menu_input_ends( UINT message )
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_TRAY_MENU_INPUT_END" ); on = !(e && e[0] == '0'); }
+    if (!on) return FALSE;
+    switch (message)
+    {
+    case WM_LBUTTONDOWN: case WM_RBUTTONDOWN: case WM_MBUTTONDOWN: case WM_XBUTTONDOWN:
+    case WM_NCLBUTTONDOWN: case WM_NCRBUTTONDOWN: case WM_NCMBUTTONDOWN: case WM_NCXBUTTONDOWN:
+    case WM_KEYDOWN: case WM_SYSKEYDOWN:
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+    return FALSE;
+}
 
 struct tray_menu_capture
 {
@@ -4783,7 +4803,7 @@
     struct systray_menu_data *data;
     COPYDATASTRUCT cds;
     UINT result = 0, size;
-    BOOL quit = FALSE;
+    BOOL quit = FALSE, back = FALSE;
     HWND tray;
     MSG msg;
 
@@ -4800,9 +4820,14 @@
     cds.dwData = WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_DATA;
     cds.cbData = size;
     cds.lpData = data;
+    NtUserSetProp( hwnd, tray_menu_activeW, ULongToHandle( request ));
     result = send_message_timeout( tray, WM_COPYDATA, (WPARAM)hwnd, (LPARAM)&cds, SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG, 2000, FALSE );
     free( data );
-    if (result != TRUE) goto failed;
+    if (result != TRUE)
+    {
+        NtUserRemoveProp( hwnd, tray_menu_activeW );
+        goto failed;
+    }
     TRACE( "menu %p (%u items) shown by the tray for %p\n", handle, c.count, hwnd );
 
     /* as in a menu loop, the application keeps running until the menu closes */
@@ -4827,11 +4852,18 @@
                 quit = TRUE;
                 break;
             }
+            if (tray_menu_input_ends( msg.message ))
+            {
+                TRACE( "input %#x in %p: the tray's menu is gone\n", msg.message, msg.hwnd );
+                back = TRUE;
+            }
             NtUserTranslateMessage( &msg, 0 );
             NtUserDispatchMessage( &msg );
+            if (back) break;
         }
-        if (quit) break;
+        if (quit || back) break;
     }
+    if (is_window( hwnd )) NtUserRemoveProp( hwnd, tray_menu_activeW );
 
     *ret = (flags & TPM_RETURNCMD) ? 0 : TRUE;
     if (result && result <= c.count && is_window( hwnd ))
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_sni.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_sni.c
@@ -214,6 +214,8 @@
 static UINT sni_menu_counter;
 static const WCHAR menu_propW[] = WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_PROP_INIT;
 static const WCHAR menu_resultW[] = WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_RESULT_PROP_INIT;
+static const WCHAR menu_activeW[] = WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_ACTIVE_PROP_INIT;
+static const WCHAR app_nameW[] = WINE_SYSTRAY_APP_NAME_PROP_INIT;
 
 static BOOL sni_dbusmenu_enabled(void)
 {
@@ -1025,6 +1027,13 @@
 /* end the application's TrackPopupMenu: value is the item index + 1, 0 for none; called without sni_mutex */
 static void finish_app_menu( HWND owner, UINT request, UINT value )
 {
+    /* NEUTRON tray-host-polish: an application that left the menu by itself (the user clicked or typed in it, see
+     * win32u menu.c) takes no result; one left behind would hold back its next menu */
+    if (HandleToUlong( NtUserGetProp( owner, menu_activeW )) != request)
+    {
+        TRACE( "menu request %u of %p: the application already left it\n", request, owner );
+        return;
+    }
     TRACE( "menu request %u of %p ends with item %u\n", request, owner, value );
     NtUserSetProp( owner, menu_resultW, ULongToHandle( MAKELONG( value, request )));
     NtUserPostMessage( owner, WM_NULL, 0, 0 );
@@ -1424,6 +1433,35 @@
     memcpy( copy, data, data->size );
 
     pthread_mutex_lock( &sni_mutex );
+    if (!data->request)
+    {
+        /* NEUTRON tray-host-polish: the program's last menu, remembered by explorer: the layout the tray holds before
+         * the first click (a tray that draws the menu sizes it from that layout), replaced at every click */
+        LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( icon, &sni_icons, struct sni_icon, entry )
+        {
+            if ((UINT)(UINT_PTR)icon->owner != (UINT)(UINT_PTR)hwnd || icon->menu.data || !icon->conn ||
+                !icon->use_dbusmenu) continue;
+            if (icon->menu.state != MENU_IDLE) continue;
+            icon->menu.data = copy;
+            copy = NULL;
+            revision = ++icon->menu.revision;
+            conn = p_dbus_connection_ref( icon->conn );
+            break;
+        }
+        pthread_mutex_unlock( &sni_mutex );
+        free( copy );
+        if (!conn) return FALSE;
+        TRACE( "remembered menu of %p, %u items, revision %u\n", hwnd, data->count, revision );
+        if ((signal = p_dbus_message_new_signal( DBUSMENU_PATH, DBUSMENU_INTERFACE, "LayoutUpdated" )))
+        {
+            p_dbus_message_append_args( signal, DBUS_TYPE_UINT32, &revision, DBUS_TYPE_INT32, &root, DBUS_TYPE_INVALID );
+            p_dbus_connection_send( conn, signal, NULL );
+            p_dbus_message_unref( signal );
+        }
+        p_dbus_connection_unref( conn );
+        sni_wakeup();
+        return TRUE;
+    }
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( icon, &sni_icons, struct sni_icon, entry )
     {
         if (icon->menu.state != MENU_WAITING || icon->menu.click_pending || !icon->conn) continue;
@@ -2230,12 +2268,30 @@
             {
                 /* NEUTRON tray-menus-v2: the notification's application name: the first line of the icon's tip (tray
                  * applications put their name there), as Windows shows the application's name, not an id */
-                char app[128];
+                char app[128] = "";
                 const char *nl;
-                pthread_mutex_lock( &sni_mutex );
-                snprintf( app, sizeof(app), "%s", icon->tip && icon->tip[0] ? icon->tip : icon->item_id );
-                pthread_mutex_unlock( &sni_mutex );
-                if ((nl = strchr( app, '\n' ))) app[nl - app] = 0;
+                char *name;
+                /* NEUTRON tray-host-polish: the program's name from its version info (explorer, ntuser.h), as
+                 * Windows names a toast's application; else the first line of the tip */
+                ATOM atom = HandleToUlong( NtUserGetProp( nid->hWnd, app_nameW ));
+                if (atom)
+                {
+                    char buf[sizeof(ATOM_BASIC_INFORMATION) + 256 * sizeof(WCHAR)];
+                    ATOM_BASIC_INFORMATION *abi = (ATOM_BASIC_INFORMATION *)buf;
+                    if (!NtQueryInformationAtom( atom, AtomBasicInformation, abi, sizeof(buf), NULL ) &&
+                        abi->NameLength && (name = utf8_from_wide( abi->Name, abi->NameLength / sizeof(WCHAR) )))
+                    {
+                        snprintf( app, sizeof(app), "%s", name );
+                        free( name );
+                    }
+                }
+                if (!app[0])
+                {
+                    pthread_mutex_lock( &sni_mutex );
+                    snprintf( app, sizeof(app), "%s", icon->tip && icon->tip[0] ? icon->tip : icon->item_id );
+                    pthread_mutex_unlock( &sni_mutex );
+                    if ((nl = strchr( app, '\n' ))) app[nl - app] = 0;
+                }
                 if (!app[0]) snprintf( app, sizeof(app), "%s", icon->item_id );
                 id = show_balloon( old, app, nid, argb, w, h );
             }
--- a/include/ntuser.h
+++ b/include/ntuser.h
@@ -701,6 +701,16 @@
     {'_','_','w','i','n','e','_','s','y','s','t','r','a','y','_','m','e','n','u',0}
 #define WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_RESULT_PROP_INIT \
     {'_','_','w','i','n','e','_','s','y','s','t','r','a','y','_','m','e','n','u','_','r','e','s','u','l','t',0}
+/* NEUTRON tray-host-polish: while TrackPopupMenu waits for the tray's answer it sets WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_ACTIVE_PROP to
+ * the request; the shell sets the result only while it matches. Some trays never report that the menu closed; the
+ * application then leaves the wait by itself (result 0) when the user clicks or types in it, the menu being gone.
+ * A menu with request 0 is a program's last menu remembered by explorer, the tray's starting layout for its icon.
+ * WINE_SYSTRAY_APP_NAME_PROP on an icon's window is a global atom with the program's name (its version info), for
+ * the notifications of its balloons. */
+#define WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_ACTIVE_PROP_INIT \
+    {'_','_','w','i','n','e','_','s','y','s','t','r','a','y','_','m','e','n','u','_','a','c','t','i','v','e',0}
+#define WINE_SYSTRAY_APP_NAME_PROP_INIT \
+    {'_','_','w','i','n','e','_','s','y','s','t','r','a','y','_','a','p','p','_','n','a','m','e',0}
 
 struct systray_menu_item
 {
--- a/programs/explorer/Makefile.in
+++ b/programs/explorer/Makefile.in
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 MODULE    = explorer.exe
 IMPORTS   = rpcrt4 user32 gdi32 advapi32 win32u
-DELAYIMPORTS = comctl32 shell32 oleaut32 ole32 shlwapi
+DELAYIMPORTS = comctl32 shell32 oleaut32 ole32 shlwapi version
 
 EXTRADLLFLAGS = -mwindows -municode
 
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -843,6 +843,112 @@
     }
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON tray-host-polish ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
+
+/* the full path of the program that owns a window */
+static BOOL get_window_program( HWND hwnd, WCHAR *path, DWORD size )
+{
+    DWORD pid = 0;
+    HANDLE process;
+    BOOL ret;
+
+    if (!GetWindowThreadProcessId( hwnd, &pid ) || !pid) return FALSE;
+    if (!(process = OpenProcess( PROCESS_QUERY_LIMITED_INFORMATION, FALSE, pid ))) return FALSE;
+    ret = QueryFullProcessImageNameW( process, 0, path, &size );
+    CloseHandle( process );
+    return ret;
+}
+
+/* Windows names a tray balloon's (toast's) application by its version info, not by an id: the program's
+ * FileDescription, else its ProductName, else the file name. Kept on the icon's window as a global atom for the
+ * display driver (WINE_SYSTRAY_APP_NAME_PROP, ntuser.h). */
+static void set_tray_app_name( HWND hwnd )
+{
+    static const WCHAR propW[] = WINE_SYSTRAY_APP_NAME_PROP_INIT;
+    static const WCHAR transW[] = L"\\VarFileInfo\\Translation";
+    static const WCHAR *const fields[] = { L"FileDescription", L"ProductName" };
+    WCHAR path[MAX_PATH], query[64], name[256] = L"", *value, *p;
+    struct { WORD lang, codepage; } *trans;
+    UINT len, i;
+    DWORD size;
+    void *info = NULL;
+    ATOM atom;
+
+    if (GetPropW( hwnd, propW ) || !get_window_program( hwnd, path, ARRAY_SIZE(path) )) return;
+    if ((size = GetFileVersionInfoSizeW( path, NULL )) && (info = malloc( size )) &&
+        GetFileVersionInfoW( path, 0, size, info ) &&
+        VerQueryValueW( info, transW, (void **)&trans, &len ) && len >= sizeof(*trans))
+    {
+        for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(fields) && !name[0]; i++)
+        {
+            swprintf( query, ARRAY_SIZE(query), L"\\StringFileInfo\\%04x%04x\\%s", trans->lang, trans->codepage,
+                      fields[i] );
+            if (VerQueryValueW( info, query, (void **)&value, &len ) && len && value[0])
+                lstrcpynW( name, value, ARRAY_SIZE(name) );
+        }
+    }
+    free( info );
+    if (!name[0])
+    {
+        p = wcsrchr( path, '\\' );
+        lstrcpynW( name, p ? p + 1 : path, ARRAY_SIZE(name) );
+        if ((p = wcsrchr( name, '.' ))) *p = 0;
+    }
+    if (name[0] && (atom = GlobalAddAtomW( name ))) SetPropW( hwnd, propW, ULongToHandle( atom ));
+}
+
+/* A tray that draws a program's menu itself (dbusmenu: XFCE's panel, waybar) sizes the menu from the layout it holds
+ * when the user clicks, before the program can be asked (Windows asks the program only then), so a first menu was a
+ * one-row popup with a scroll arrow. explorer keeps each program's last menu (HKCU\Software\Wine\Explorer\TrayMenus,
+ * by program path) and hands it to the display driver when the program's icon comes back: the tray's starting layout.
+ * The program's own menu still replaces it at every click. Kill switch NEUTRON_TRAY_MENU_MEMORY=0. */
+static BOOL tray_menu_memory(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0)
+    {
+        WCHAR buf[8];
+        on = !(GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"NEUTRON_TRAY_MENU_MEMORY", buf, ARRAY_SIZE(buf) ) && buf[0] == '0');
+    }
+    return on;
+}
+
+static void remember_tray_menu( HWND hwnd, const struct systray_menu_data *menu )
+{
+    WCHAR path[MAX_PATH];
+    HKEY key;
+
+    if (!tray_menu_memory() || !get_window_program( hwnd, path, ARRAY_SIZE(path) )) return;
+    if (RegCreateKeyExW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Software\\Wine\\Explorer\\TrayMenus", 0, NULL, 0, KEY_SET_VALUE, NULL,
+                         &key, NULL )) return;
+    RegSetValueExW( key, path, 0, REG_BINARY, (const BYTE *)menu, menu->size );
+    RegCloseKey( key );
+}
+
+static void replay_tray_menu( HWND hwnd )
+{
+    struct systray_menu_data *menu;
+    WCHAR path[MAX_PATH];
+    DWORD size = 0, type;
+    HKEY key;
+
+    if (!tray_menu_memory() || !get_window_program( hwnd, path, ARRAY_SIZE(path) )) return;
+    if (RegOpenKeyExW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Software\\Wine\\Explorer\\TrayMenus", 0, KEY_QUERY_VALUE, &key )) return;
+    if (!RegQueryValueExW( key, path, NULL, &type, NULL, &size ) && type == REG_BINARY &&
+        size >= offsetof( struct systray_menu_data, items[1] ) && (menu = malloc( size )))
+    {
+        if (!RegQueryValueExW( key, path, NULL, NULL, (BYTE *)menu, &size ) && menu->size == size && menu->count &&
+            menu->count <= (size - offsetof( struct systray_menu_data, items )) / sizeof(menu->items[0]))
+        {
+            menu->request = 0;
+            NtUserMessageCall( hwnd, WINE_SYSTRAY_NOTIFY_ICON, WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_DATA, 0, menu,
+                               NtUserSystemTrayCall, FALSE );
+        }
+        free( menu );
+    }
+    RegCloseKey( key );
+}
+
 static BOOL handle_incoming(HWND hwndSource, COPYDATASTRUCT *cds)
 {
     struct icon *icon = NULL;
@@ -859,8 +965,11 @@
             !menu->count || menu->count > (cds->cbData - offsetof( struct systray_menu_data, items )) /
                                           sizeof(menu->items[0]))
             return FALSE;
-        return NtUserMessageCall( hwndSource, WINE_SYSTRAY_NOTIFY_ICON, WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_DATA, 0,
-                                  (void *)menu, NtUserSystemTrayCall, FALSE ) == TRUE;
+        if (NtUserMessageCall( hwndSource, WINE_SYSTRAY_NOTIFY_ICON, WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_DATA, 0,
+                               (void *)menu, NtUserSystemTrayCall, FALSE ) != TRUE)
+            return FALSE;
+        remember_tray_menu( hwndSource, menu );
+        return TRUE;
     }
 
     if (cds->cbData < sizeof(*data)) return FALSE;
@@ -920,12 +1029,16 @@
         nid.hBalloonIcon = CreateIcon(NULL, data->balloon_icon_info.width, data->balloon_icon_info.height, data->balloon_icon_info.planes, data->balloon_icon_info.bpp,
                                       icon_data, icon_data + cbMaskBits);
     }
+    if ((nid.uFlags & NIF_INFO) && nid.szInfo[0]) set_tray_app_name( nid.hWnd );
     /* try forwarding to the display driver first */
     if (cds->dwData == NIM_ADD || !(icon = get_icon( nid.hWnd, nid.uID )))
     {
         if ((ret = NtUserMessageCall( hwndSource, WINE_SYSTRAY_NOTIFY_ICON, cds->dwData, 0,
                                       &nid, NtUserSystemTrayCall, FALSE )) != -1)
+        {
+            if (cds->dwData == NIM_ADD && ret) replay_tray_menu( nid.hWnd );
             goto done;
+        }
         ret = FALSE;
     }
 
